  "defects": [
    "A voltage failure report can fail during delivery after the KMD rejects a rail vote. Dropping the vote at that point leaves the provider awaiting the same generation, including its two-second timeout.",
    "Completing provider removal and reopening an instance reuses the namespace for voltage requests. An empty mailbox used to drop the retained floor. A reused word could also match the old acknowledgement and suppress the new notification."
  ],
  "repair": [
    "Retry an undelivered failure report on the next regular policy poll for the same request and provider. Preserve the rail result and skip further attempts on a permanently unsupported notification.",
    "Bind query and notification to the referenced provider instance, change generation on completed removal or close, keep it across canceled removal and retain the prior voltage floor until the next explicit vote."
  ],
